  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 236 PM EDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThursday through Monday...\n\n\nEarly fall weather is here! This pattern should last throughout \nMonday(ish) before our heat starts to creep back in. We remain in a \nlight northeasterly flow at the surface, due to an upper level \nblocking pattern centered over southern Ontario. As we aren't \npulling moisture from the Gulf, we will see lower dew points and RH \nvalues and remain mostly dry. On Thursday and Friday, expect to see \nhighs in the low 70s, with overnight lows in the upper 40s and low \n50s. Saturday morning is expected to be the chilliest of all, \nheading closer to low 40s across the region before starting our slow \nreturn to warmer temps. Expect sprinkles and the occasional shower \nfrom Thursday through Sunday, but long periods of rain aren't in the \nforecast. Lower clouds in the overnights and fog in the mornings is \nlikely, but should be mostly clear skies throughout the day Thursday \nthrough Sunday. \n\nMonday and Tuesday push back up toward the upper 70s as a high temp \nacross the Bluegrass region with a gradient to the mid 80s toward \nthe Bowling Green Area. As we heat up next week, we should still get \na good diurnal cycle and cool to the upper 50s, bringing plenty of \nrelief and letting us continue our fall hopes and dreams.",
